<!--
  VINTF device compatibility matrix for the bare-metal x86_64 PC target.

  This declares what the VENDOR image requires of the FRAMEWORK -- the opposite
  direction from manifest.xml, which declares what the vendor provides.

  Intentionally empty: during bring-up the vendor side requires nothing
  specific of the framework. checkvintf still needs the file to exist
  (getDeviceCompatibilityMatrix fails with -2 if it is missing), so an empty
  matrix is the correct answer rather than an omitted file.

  Add <hal optional="false"> entries here only when a vendor component genuinely
  cannot function without a given framework HAL.
-->
<compatibility-matrix version="1.0" type="device">

</compatibility-matrix>
